Q: Find document with array that contains a specific value A: <p>Though I agree with find() is most effective in your use case, still there is $match of the aggregation framework, to ease the query of a big number of entries and generate a low number of results that hold value to you, especially for grouping and creating new files.</p>
<blockquote>
<pre><code>  PersonModel.aggregate([
            {
                 &quot;$match&quot;: {
                     $and : [{ 'favouriteFoods' : { $exists: true, $in: [ 'sushi']}}, ........ ]  }
             },
             { $project : {&quot;_id&quot;: 0, &quot;name&quot; : 1} }
            ]);
</code></pre>
</blockquote>

Q: Unable to hit API after application is hosted on IIS A: <p>I experienced the same problem but mine was for laravel 12.</p>
<p>I created a <code>web.config</code> file in the <code>public folder</code></p>
<pre><code>&lt;?xml version=&quot;1.0&quot; encoding=&quot;UTF-8&quot;?&gt;
&lt;configuration&gt;
  &lt;system.webServer&gt;
    &lt;rewrite&gt;
      &lt;rules&gt;
        &lt;rule name=&quot;Routing&quot; stopProcessing=&quot;true&quot;&gt;
          &lt;match url=&quot;.*&quot; /&gt;
          &lt;conditions&gt;
            &lt;add input=&quot;{REQUEST_FILENAME}&quot; matchType=&quot;IsFile&quot; negate=&quot;true&quot; /&gt;
            &lt;add input=&quot;{REQUEST_FILENAME}&quot; matchType=&quot;IsDirectory&quot; negate=&quot;true&quot; /&gt;
          &lt;/conditions&gt;
          &lt;action type=&quot;Rewrite&quot; url=&quot;index.php&quot; /&gt;
        &lt;/rule&gt;
      &lt;/rules&gt;
    &lt;/rewrite&gt;
  &lt;/system.webServer&gt;
&lt;/configuration&gt;

⚠️ Without this:

/api/* routes will NOT work

You’ll get 404 on all routes except /
</code></pre>

Q: How to have a default value for a dashboard page widgets filter in Filament 4? A: <p>The filters form is indeed special here and <strong>ignores default values set on any inputs (DatePicker, TextInput,...)</strong>.</p>
<p>You can however <strong>achieve your desired behavior by conditionally initializing the Livewire component properties</strong> in the <a href="https://livewire.laravel.com/docs/3.x/lifecycle-hooks#mount" rel="nofollow noreferrer"><code>mount()</code> lifecycle hook method</a> (called when the Livewire component is created):</p>
<pre class="lang-php prettyprint-override"><code>class Dashboard extends BaseDashboard
{
    use HasFiltersForm;

    ...

    public function mount(): void
    {
        // The default values here precede the ones in the Filament/Helper/DateHelper
        $this-&gt;filters['startDate'] ??= now()-&gt;startOfYear()-&gt;toDateString();
        $this-&gt;filters['endDate']   ??= now()-&gt;endOfYear()-&gt;toDateString();
    }
}
</code></pre>
<blockquote>
<p>Remember: &quot;<a href="https://filamentphp.com/docs/4.x/getting-started#custom-pages" rel="nofollow noreferrer">every page class in a Filament panel is a Livewire component</a>&quot;.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>The <code>??=</code> (null coalescing assignment operator) prevents overwriting the value if the user already selected a date (he might just reload the page).</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Note: in the dashboard class that defines the page filters, the variable is called <code>$this-&gt;filters</code>. Only in the widgets classes that interact with it it's <code>$this-&gt;pageFilters</code>.</p>
</blockquote>
